content.text:
There's also the vent/hazard etc. Fine.

Add solidMeshes for generators? did. For barriers? did. Core? did. AC? did. Crates and barrels. Floor. Good. Maybe railings not shot; floor boundary. Fine.

Wait, core `g.position.set(0,0,-18)` after meshes added to g; solidMeshes holds children with world transform through parent, raycaster handles matrices. Fine.

Now main.js.

Important details for import paths: `three/addons/postprocessing/EffectComposer.js` maps to vendor/postprocessing/... because importmap `three/addons/` -> `./vendor/`. So EffectComposer imports `../shaders/...` resolves `vendor/shaders`, correct. But it imports 'three' resolved. Good.

Let's write main.js. Include error handling.

Outline:

```js
import * as THREE from 'three';
import { EffectComposer } from 'three/addons/postprocessing/EffectComposer.js';
...
import { World } ...
```

Startup:
```
const canvas = document.getElementById('game');
const renderer = new THREE.WebGLRenderer({canvas, antialias:false, powerPreference:'high-performance', stencil:false});
renderer.outputColorSpace = THREE.SRGBColorSpace;
renderer.toneMapping = THREE.ACESFilmicToneMapping;
renderer.toneMappingExposure = 1.12;
renderer.setPixelRatio(Math.min(devicePixelRatio, isTouch?1.5:1.6));
renderer.setSize(innerWidth, innerHeight);
renderer.shadowMap.enabled = !low; type PCFSoft;
```

detect renderer:
```
const gl=renderer.getContext(); const dbg=gl.getExtension('WEBGL_debug_renderer_info'); const rendererName=...
const software=/swiftshader|llvmpipe|software/i.test(rendererName)
```

Quality: pixel ratio = software ? 1 : min(dpr,1.75). Low = software || isTouch with dpr? Touch devices high res; cap 1.5. Actually low only software; mobile maybe medium. Use `quality = software ? 0 : (isTouch ? 1 : 2)`. Set bloom strength maybe. We'll show readout.

Scene, camera.
World = new World(scene, renderer, {low: software}); builds.
fx, audio, player, weapon, hud, enemies.
camera.add(weapon.root) inside Weapon constructor.
scene.add(camera).

Composer:
```
